% An argument that needs the statement the term is already proving at
% that point (tasks.org, aida-circular-supporter-judged-in).
%
%   pro   : B from an obligation for A
%   back  : A from an obligation for B   (circular inside B's debate)
%   other : A from a presumption of D    (a genuine supporter of A)
%
% B is IN (via other).  With back registered last it is on top of A's
% stack; sigma judges it IN (its source B is IN) and keeps it, although
% inside B's debate back's B can only be an obligation: the evaluation
% is OPEN.  With other registered last it is VALUE.
lk.
declare A,B,D:bool.
declare r1: (A -> B).
declare r3: (B -> A).
declare rd: (D -> A).

argument pro : (B).
cut (A -> B) th.
axiom r1.
elim.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

argument other : (A).
cut (D -> A) th.
axiom rd.
elim.
by default.
next.
axiom.
dixi.

argument back : (A).
cut (B -> A) th.
axiom r3.
elim.
next.
axiom.
dixi.
